<Base title="Rectifier Model Scope & Disclaimer" description="Read the limits of filtered bridge estimates and ideal rectifier averages, including excluded circuit behavior, component ratings, and regulator effects."><div class="shell page-intro legal"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Disclaimer' }]} /><h1>Know what the estimate means.</h1><div class="prose"><h2>Educational circuit models</h2><p>This calculator estimates selected rectifier quantities for sinusoidal single-phase input. Filtered mode assumes a constant-current load, fixed diode drops, and small approximately linear ripple. Unfiltered modes assume ideal diodes and a resistive load.</p><h2>Excluded behavior</h2><p>The model omits transformer regulation and resistance, changing diode characteristics, capacitor ESR and tolerance, inrush, transient loads, and regulator behavior. It does not predict regulated adapter output, available load current, component ratings, efficiency, or electrical safety.</p><h2>Precision and interpretation</h2><p>Displayed digits reflect numerical formatting, not physical accuracy. A 20% ripple guardrail limits the selected approximation's scope; it is not a certified error bound. Practical decisions require suitable measurements, specifications, and qualified assessment.</p><h2>References and corrections</h2><p>Read the <a href="/ac-to-dc-calculator/#formula">formulas and references</a>. Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> to prepare a reproducible calculation report.</p></div></div></Base>
